WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.800 --> 00:00:05.960
A motorcycle would solve most of my problems.

00:00:11.420 --> 00:00:15.880
Zombies are getting faster every day, making it hard to scavenge on foot.

00:00:19.760 --> 00:00:22.800
It would be easier with two people.

00:00:26.500 --> 00:00:31.560
But holding down the fort is also an important job, which my roommate has volunteered to do.

00:00:32.300 --> 00:00:36.220
He performs best when not hungry and seated by a fire.

00:00:40.720 --> 00:00:44.480
This is where I planted my chopsticks yesterday.

00:00:45.280 --> 00:00:49.460
I will make the bike frame out of this bamboo.

00:01:02.360 --> 00:01:07.960
Crafting is much easier with blueprints because they guide where all the pieces go.

00:01:14.220 --> 00:01:19.740
Cloth strips bind the bamboo together. Be aware - you cannot reverse this process.

00:01:25.880 --> 00:01:29.640
Before I learned how to make cloth strips, I had clothes.

00:01:37.460 --> 00:01:44.040
For additional strips, I considered using my final article of clothing. But since I don’t know VFX I can’t blur out my genitals for this video.

00:02:02.300 --> 00:02:04.280
Munchkin tombstones.

00:02:08.620 --> 00:02:11.980
Crafting wheels starts with a clay hub and spokes.

00:02:16.840 --> 00:02:21.720
Sorry about the background. Bitch boy decided to interrupt and remodel.

00:02:31.720 --> 00:02:36.120
To absorb shock, we need to create a tire. The fresher, the better.

00:02:46.700 --> 00:02:51.360
The recipe requires three arms and four  cloth strips...

00:02:59.320 --> 00:03:04.520
Holding hands in perfect harmony. Reminds me when we used to pray before dinner.

00:03:15.560 --> 00:03:17.220
Very satisfying.

00:03:24.880 --> 00:03:28.100
I never thought I would live this long.

00:03:32.180 --> 00:03:35.260
I must do dangerous things to survive.

00:03:52.460 --> 00:03:55.660
But sometimes I make other people do them for me.

00:03:57.240 --> 00:04:02.520
We need to power the bike with an engine. This sturdy log will be our engine block.

00:04:15.340 --> 00:04:20.380
The peaceful quiet of the forest plays a big part in inspiring my creations.

00:04:29.940 --> 00:04:33.540
The sound of the wind keeps me sane in troubling times.

00:04:45.640 --> 00:04:50.580
Combining coal powder and gypsum crystals will fuel our engine.

00:04:57.780 --> 00:04:59.940
Don't add too much magic gypsum!

00:05:11.540 --> 00:05:16.820
Looks like the zombies hate noise as much as I do. Next time I’ll try solar power.

00:05:18.540 --> 00:05:20.220
Time to bust some skulls.

00:05:25.840 --> 00:05:28.260
Now it's time to scavenge!!!

00:05:28.680 --> 00:05:30.880
I'm going to get so much stuff.

00:05:32.300 --> 00:05:36.960
Look at how cool this looks when I ride it around camp!

00:05:39.060 --> 00:05:42.120
Good luck "holding down the fort" !

00:06:01.080 --> 00:06:02.360
They see me rollin.

00:06:04.660 --> 00:06:07.300
The best crystals are in the sewers, beneath the old city.

00:06:08.360 --> 00:06:12.620
I sometimes wonder what it must of been like to live here in the golden days.

00:06:20.420 --> 00:06:22.260
This would make a great hat.

00:06:24.280 --> 00:06:27.360
Six inches under. My munchkin brothers RIP.

00:06:32.080 --> 00:06:36.000
This is where I lost my stuff earlier. Now I’m unstoppable!

00:06:42.300 --> 00:06:47.340
If my Meemaw taught me anything, it was never leave a family member behind.

00:06:52.720 --> 00:06:55.360
Or my camera, since that’s how I make these videos.

